The proposed Logan Indoor Sports Centre (LISC) has been identified as a host venue for the 2032 Brisbane Olympic and Paralympic Games (the Games) and will be located within Logan Central which is the cultural and civic heart of Logan.

LISC addresses an identified service need and provides a fit-for-purpose facility that delivers a significant uplift in the number of indoor sports courts in Logan. The venue will enhance the local area, providing economic opportunities and enhanced amenity to a rapidly growing area of south-east Queensland.

LISC will help to provide the following benefits:

- increased local sporting opportunities and pathways;

- healthier lifestyles and choices, providing improved local liveability;

- more cohesive, inclusive and safe community;

- business attraction and local employment opportunities; and

- positive Games experience for participants and spectators.

The LISC will be owned and operated by Logan City Council (LCC), delivering a lasting legacy for the region through enhanced tourism, economic development, and increased opportunities for community engagement and active recreation.

