Sunshine Coast Council is seeking a suitably qualified contractor to construct streetscaping, roadworks and a signalised crossing at, and adjacent to the intersection of Mill and Currie Streets, Nambour.

The scope of work includes, but is not limited to:

• Signalised pedestrian crossing

• Lighting

• Road pavement works

• Concrete pavement construction;

• Paved pathway construction;

• Landscaped gardens;

• Concrete driveways and kerb ramps;

• Signage and line marking;

• Kerb & channel works;

• Stormwater drainage works;

• Supply and Installation of precast islands;

• Public utility alterations.

Council will appoint a Certifying Engineer in accordance with the requirements of the TMR conditional approval and a superintendent to assess and certify claims, EOT’s and variations.

As required by TMR’s prequalification system guidelines, all works within the State Controlled Road (SCR) boundaries valued in excess of $300,000 shall be carried out by a Local Authority or a Contractor, prequalified under the National Prequalification System.

For this project contractors are required to hold a minimum TMR prequalification of R2 B1 F5.

A site information session will not be held for this Tender. Respondents are to carry out their own due diligence in relation to familiarising with the site.

This is a lump sum Contract. The successful Contractor will be required to provide all materials, plant and labour to perform all necessary operations of whatever kind, to ensure the completion of works associated with this Contract.

Council will be awarding the contract prior to end of year 2026, with the awarded Contractor required to commence as soon as practicable following award. If an early 2027 site establishment date is nominated this must be clearly communicated in the submission response. A six month construction period has been communicated to the community.

