vendorPanelDetails.background:
Townsville Hospital and Health Service requires the supply of radiation oncology treatment equipment to support the delivery of safe, effective and contemporary cancer treatment services.

The existing equipment has reached end of life and must be replaced to support the continued delivery of radiation oncology services.

The Supplier must ensure that the offered equipment is:

(a)	fit for purpose;

(b)	clinically operational;

(c)	compliant with all applicable standards and regulatory requirements; and

(d)	capable of safe and reliable integration into the existing radiation oncology service environment.

The Supplier must liaise and coordinate with the Customer, project stakeholders, building stakeholders and any other relevant parties throughout delivery, installation, acceptance and transition into service.

